# Who owns what, and why it is a file rather than a convention
#
# A path a human "owns" informally is a path nobody reviews, and the eleven personas in
# `.github/agents/` are a review vocabulary that already exists — the review ruleset maps
# every finding category onto one of them. So the same personas own the paths, and an
# automated assistant role and a human review role resolve to the same owner rather than
# to two people who read the same diff.
#
# The `@` form is what GitHub requires; the trailing comments are the readable half and
# GitHub ignores them. They are kept in sync with `.github/review-rules/rules.json`, whose
# `categories` map is the authority: a persona that owns a path but appears in no
# category is an owner nobody assigns findings to.

# The default. Every path is owned by somebody; a file that matches nothing below falls
# to the principal architect, who is the persona the review vocabulary already sends
# every `Complexity` and `Boundary design` finding to.
*                               @sergey-bar

